<!--
    Kuna `xnutables` option (P1 external refinement): kalloc_type views and
    IOExternalMethodDispatch tables on an XNU kext.

    The fixture (gen_iokit.py) adds to the iokitclasses kext one
    __kalloc_type view for site.Derived (signature 121112, 0x30 bytes), a
    four-record IOExternalMethodDispatch table whose address Derived's own
    vtable method computes, alloc_derived (allocates through kalloc_type_impl
    and stores into the result) and a reader of the table's third function
    pointer. Only the allocator and alloc_derived have symbols.

    Pass 1 (`option xnutables off`) is the bug: the view is a bare address,
    the dispatched handler is sub_<addr>, the allocation is a long with casts
    around it and the table read is dat_<addr>. Pass 2 (`on`) names the view
    kalloc_type_view_Derived and the handler after its owner and selector,
    types the allocation Derived * from the view's signature (field_0x18 a
    pointer, field_0x8 data) and the table IOExternalMethodDispatch[4].
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c0035fd6</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
